a car engine maybe to blame for starting  a garage fire in a family's home in the  Northwest Valley well Mary Jane beliesa  shares how the family wants to spread  awareness and hopes others will be more  vigilant  this is what's left of the Siever  family's home after a garage fire broke  out Friday evening you just don't ever  expect your car to you know self-implode  and explode Cody Sharp's young daughter  alerted her father Uncle Eli and  grandmother Dory Siever after hearing a  popping noise coming from the garage  garage door it was a wall of fire it's  it looked like a dragon was in my garage  and that it hit me pretty hard and I  knew that there was no saving it so I  grabbed my daughter and left with no  time to react and just the clothes on  their back the family grabbed the pets  and ran out the front door as far as the  firefighters are concerned they they  were fairly adamant that that was that  was probably the cause and the car had  been off for hours it's not like we had  just pulled in and left the car running  I hope that's not the case I really hope  that the vehicle did not cause the  entire house to burn down because that  would be worth one and it would put a  lot of people at risk a lot of people  with a similar vehicle and this is not  an old vehicle it's not a 1990s vehicle  this is a 2019 Chevy tracks Victor  botanari owner of universal motor car  says while car engine fires are uncommon  that's most likely it's from an  electrical problem it can still happen  and a routine inspection may help other  technician to check for leaks make sure  everything gets good check the take a  quick look at the wiring harness and  things like this and I don't recommend  install aftermarket systems the family  as well it's not easy to pick up the  pieces it's easy knowing they are  thankful to have survived and still have  each other it's horrible it's hard you  know photos and and things you just  can't replace that's that's the roughest  part but everything is replaceable the  Siever family tells me the investigation  is still ongoing and will take up to a  few weeks reporting from Craig and  Rancho Mary June bellezza 8 News Now
 

